Dear Mr Moss,

A contractor has now looked at the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews. His findings: the coating is flaking on the flat-side face and there is a rub mark at the upper edge. The door leaf touches the frame at the top as it closes, and it latches when pulled shut. He did not remove hardware, measure clearances, inspect the door's construction or test its fire performance, so the cause of the catching is not yet known.

You asked whether this could be limited to decorating. On these findings we cannot say that. The leaf touching the frame is not a paint problem on its face, and the building file lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting. The painting quote (Pale Finch Decorating, £186.00) covers painting only and says nothing about the catching or the fire rating.

I have sent you a separate approval request with the options: painting only at £186.00; a further inspection of the closing, clearances and hinges by a door specialist, with the price to come to you first; or both. Please tell us which you would like. Nothing further will go ahead without your approval, and no drilling or alteration will be done without checking with building management.

You asked for a price before any chargeable work. We have not yet been told whether the visit already made carries a charge, and no cost was approved before it. We have asked the contractor and will tell you the amount if there is one. The decision on payment will be yours.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings
